{title: Mourning into Dancing}
{subtitle: Psalms 30:12–13}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 98}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | [C] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [A] | [A] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]I was dressed in sackcloth
Sitting in the dust
[C]But you came and lifted me
You turned it all around [Bb][A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]You turned my mourning into dancing
[C]You clothed me with joy
[Bb]My heart will sing your praise
And not be silent
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Take a[Dm]way my sorrow
Put the music in my feet
Lord, my God, I [C]thank you
Forever I will sing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You turned my mourning in[Dm]to dancing
You clothed me with joy
My heart will [C]sing your praise
And not be [Bb]silent
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Baila, baila, dance before the Lord
[A]I will [Dm]thank you forever
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You turned my mourning in[C]to dancing
You clothed me [Bb]with joy
My heart will sing your praise
And not be [A]silent [Dm]
{end_of_chorus}
